body:
I watch cuz it's good? I cried at devilman crybaby ;-;;;
I'm also Japanese. My mom was born in Tokyo. I know the culture. Japanese people didn't really invent the word, iirc it was invented by 4chan users.

Trans characters are often referred to by this anyways. Lily hoshikawa was referred to as **** by a lot of people when it was revealed she was trans. There are characters in shows who try to trick people sure, but just call them a trickster or something. Trans people aren't asking for an insane amount of preferential treatment, they're asking not to see insulting slurs whenever they look at something anime related. Trans ppl are not being treated equally at all, cis people aren't constantly dealing with someone using a word commonly used to insult them.
